/P 76 0 R
/E (Smart Traffic Control is one of the most prominent real-world applications of multi-agent systems. Autonomous and semi-autonomous vehicles must coordinate at intersections without centralized control, naturally giving rise to game-theoretic interactions. Traditional signal-timing approaches are static and reactive; a game-theoretic approach enables agents to adapt, anticipate, and reason about each other's behavior. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
