447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 78 0 R
/T (The Smart Traffic game is modelled as a simultaneous-move, two-player normal-form game. Each agent independently chooses between two routes: SHORT \(the direct but potentially congested route\) and LONG \(the alternative route\). The payoff matrix captures the utility each agent receives from every combination of choices. )
/E (The Smart Traffic game is modelled as a simultaneous-move, two-player normal-form game. Each agent independently chooses between two routes: SHORT \(the direct but potentially congested route\) and LONG \(the alternative route\). The payoff matrix captures the utility each agent receives from every combination of choices. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 78 0 R
/T (  Payoff interpretation: When both agents take SHORT, congestion reduces utility to \(5, 5\). If  one deviatesto LONG while the other takes SHORT, the SHORT agent benefits greatly \(8\)  while theLONG agent suffers \(2\). Both choosing LONG yields a moderate \(6, 6\). This structure  resemblesacoordination game with asymmetric mixed incentives. )
/E (  Payoff interpretation: When both agents take SHORT, congestion reduces utility to \(5, 5\). If  one deviatesto LONG while the other takes SHORT, the SHORT agent benefits greatly \(8\)  while theLONG agent suffers \(2\). Both choosing LONG yields a moderate \(6, 6\). This structure  resemblesacoordination game with asymmetric mixed incentives. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
